Basic
1. create .env file from .env-sample
2. run broker
    docker compose up
3. create topics through admin
    python3 admin.py
4. run consumer
    python3 consumer.py
5. publish msg
    python3 producer.py --topic {mytopic} --msg {mymessage}

Auto-add new topics
1. create new topics
2. publish trigger msg
    python3 producer.py --topic trigger --msg check-new-topics
3. consumer will resubscribe -> add new topics with paytm_ prefix. It's done on-the-fly; no downtime or new process required

Flush internal queue
>> This is to demonstrate batch insert that is triggered periodically
1. publish msg (non-trigger topic)
2. publish trigger msg
    python3 producer.py --topic trigger --msg flush
3. consumer will display previous published msgs in a "batch" (bulk_text variable) and clear internal queue.

Access broker shell script
    docker exec --workdir /opt/kafka/bin/ -it kafka-broker sh

Notes:
- Currently confluent_kafka lib is used instead of kafka-python
- Currently it's modelled for 1 consumer node only
- Ideally there should be a separate process/cronjob that sends trigger msg periodically